s created; read every stream file of the day, not only the newest, so concurrent dispatches all appear; keep the existing single-dispatch follow for seats, but when more than one dispatch is live on the day, show the seats of all live dispatches. FOUR, the Floor page: replace the placeholder text in the Queued cell with the real count and render an Up next list under the pipeline (position, purpose, repo, plan basename) and a Landed today list (purpose, status, duration, branch) with the same visual language the page already uses; the honesty watermark rules stay: the queue block is labelled as declared by the orchestrator with the added_at of the newest entry, and it never claims a queued plan is running. FIVE, Makefile targets queue-add, queue-list, queue-rm with help text, and docs/experience-data.md updated with the fleet-queue/1 schema and the new live.json fields. SIX, the now view, from data already in the stream and the plan file: for every live seat render the purpose of its plan (first comment line), the task in one line (the first sentence of that seat line in the plan file, cut at 120 characters, never the whole task body), wave x of N where N is the wave count of the plan, attempt number, elapsed time since seat_dispatch updated every second in the browser from the timestamp, and the time of the last heartbeat; a seat whose heartbeat is older than the quiet threshold is marked quiet in the same visual language the watermark uses. SEVEN, seed the queue with the plans staged today in this order and their purposes taken from each plan file header: wave-plans/assistant-channel/2026-09-11-w1c-tile.plan, wave-plans/assistant-channel/2026-09-12-w2a-iris-scaffold.plan, wave-plans/assistant-channel/2026-09-12-w2b-read-tools.plan, wave-plans/assistant-channel/2026-09-12-w2c-update-and-hosts.plan, repo olympus-platform for all four. VERIFY: python3 scripts/desk_live.py --once succeeds with the seeded queue and its output validates against the documented schema; ba